Z||000000||GT Bastard||06-27-2000||08:16 PM||||Same car... '86 3.1 w/cavalier tranny.  After installing the 3.1 motor, the engine cuts out at about 4200 rpm.  All electronics and fuel pump have been replaced(distributor, computer, coil, IAC, TPS, MAT, temp sensor, 3.8 fuel pump from a Firechicken, etc...)  Never had a problem with the stock 2.8... Currently using an '85 wiring harness and '86 computer/injectors.  Gives timing retard code.  Just curious if you fellas had any ideas.  <P>Thanks in advance.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Alex4mula||06-28-2000||10:38 AM||||Definitely must be a timing issue and not a fuel problem. Make sure that your timing mark is at 0 at TDC on #1 cyl. That should discard timing on that part.||||reg||1
